{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a33bbe8cccfe52c5ec3cd9920f71e12359f54ca09d146518a98e032b3e8b89fe","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion verifier test harness","key_entities":["tests/external/test_completion_banking_behavior_0707.py","_observe_trial","observed_upsert","CriterionBank.upsert","src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py","src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py","evidence_sufficient","seeded","record_insufficient","tests/_bank_observer.py","make_observed_upsert","tests/unit/test_completion_bank_observer_forwarding.py","verify_completion"],"problem_keywords":["signature drift","monkeypatch","keyword argument mismatch","test harness","completion verification"],"propositions":["The test monkeypatch stub observed_upsert has a narrower signature than the real CriterionBank.upsert, missing keyword-only parameters evidence_sufficient and seeded that production code passes.","The bedrock LLM arm triggers the bounded-fallback path (record_insufficient) which calls upsert with evidence_sufficient=False, causing TypeError in the narrow stub; anthropic and openai arms avoided this path by gathering sufficient evidence.","The fix threads all kwargs through the test stub via **kwargs forwarding so that evidence_sufficient, seeded, and future upsert parameters flow to the real implementation unchanged.","A shared, live-dependency-free helper make_observed_upsert extracts the observation wrapper for both live and unit tests, eliminating future signature-drift risks."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787536804922738001,"uuid":"a33221c3-83ff-4cea-a992-9f6cf4f0d70a"}